{
  "assumptions": [
    "Batch members use the same nonce and differ only in the inputs of the pattern; template precomputation (anything independent of the nonce) is free.",
    "Word-level sharing only: two members share a node only if all of its inputs are identical. Bit-level partial sharing is not modelled.",
    "Outputs needed per nonce: e60 of the outer compression (the early reject); the full digest is computed only for the rare candidates and is not counted.",
    "Cost weights are a model: primitive ops (rotate, shift, xor, and, or, add = 1) and an RDNA3 estimate (Sigma 4, sigma 4, Ch 1, Maj 2, add 1).",
    "Feasibility of each pattern follows Bitcoin consensus: version rolling has 16 free bits (BIP320), time a few thousand valid values, a merkle-tail change alone needs a 224-bit partial merkle-root collision."
  ],
  "baseline": "k = 1: every per-nonce node computed once per header (the v2 kernel's work).",
  "candidate_anomaly": false,
  "conclusion": "EXACT ANALYSIS: the counts below are exact properties of the computation, checked against the reference implementation; converting them to time uses stated cost weights unless a measurement is cited. Per-nonce work of one header with early reject: 3828 primitive ops, 2964 RDNA3 ops (exact DAG count, constants folded). version rolling (overt AsicBoost): shared 460 / per-member 2504 RDNA3 ops, k = 4 saves 11.6% time rolling: shared 4 / per-member 2960 RDNA3 ops, k = 4 saves 0.1% extranonce (new merkle root): shared 23 / per-member 2941 RDNA3 ops, k = 4 saves 0.6% version + time rolling: shared 4 / per-member 2960 RDNA3 ops, k = 4 saves 0.1% extranonce + time: shared 4 / per-member 2960 RDNA3 ops, k = 4 saves 0.1% merkle tail only (covert AsicBoost reversed): shared 23 / per-member 2941 RDNA3 ops, k = 4 saves 0.6% merkle tail + time: shared 4 / per-member 2960 RDNA3 ops, k = 4 saves 0.1% Best feasible pattern at k = 16: version rolling (overt AsicBoost), 14.5% of the per-nonce work saved (RDNA3 weights). Every saving is cost per hash; the number of hashes per block is unchanged. Deciding the target needs this share of the r-round double hash's per-nonce work (the rest is dead code once H7 = IV7 + e(r-4) is all that matters): 4 rounds 9.3%, 5 rounds 33.7%, 6 rounds 44.2%, 7 rounds 50.0%, 8 rounds 55.9%, 9 rounds 63.1%, 10 rounds 68.5%, 11 rounds 72.7%, 12 rounds 75.4%, 16 rounds 82.5%, 24 rounds 86.7%, 32 rounds 91.2%, 48 rounds 94.5%, 64 rounds 96.1%. The outer target reads inner digest words W0..W(r-4), so from 11 rounds on every inner word matters and the saving is only the early reject.",
